From: Brendan McGrath <bmcgrath@codeweavers.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mf: Don't async notify a sink that is also the time source.

Backport of WineHQ d6adaa2e59689edf0fbb3d8d6094014c442bd05c (wine-11.4).

Prerequisite of 0194: once the streaming audio renderer is the
presentation time source it is also one of the clock's state sinks,
and clock_change_state() would notify it twice, synchronously as the
time source and again asynchronously as a sink, so it would queue a
second MEStreamSinkStarted and preroll again.

Runeon adaptation: the test hunk is omitted; it removes a todo from
a test (7bff59d57c) that the base does not have. Production code is
unchanged.

diff --git a/dlls/mf/clock.c b/dlls/mf/clock.c
--- a/dlls/mf/clock.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/clock.c
@@ -642,7 +642,9 @@ static HRESULT clock_change_state(struct presentation_clock *clock, enum clock_c
 
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(sink, &clock->sinks, struct clock_sink, entry)
     {
-        clock_notify_async_sink(clock, system_time, param, notification, sink->state_sink);
+        /* Don't notify a sink that is also the time source */
+        if (clock->time_source_sink != sink->state_sink)
+            clock_notify_async_sink(clock, system_time, param, notification, sink->state_sink);
     }
 
     return S_OK;
